From d70f519e20815dc37680627a14251e708c786046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:54:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/32] fix(qsa): normalize the device key so cuda and cuda:0
 share one buffer

torch.device("cuda") and torch.device("cuda", 0) are different dict keys but the
same physical device, so the shared packed-KV plan minted a SECOND max-size buffer
for the bare form and silently halved the saving. The forward path always passes
k_buffer.device, which carries an index, but a reservation or a caller that builds
the device by name does not.

Found by the GPU2 equivalence run, which reported packed_allocations=2 and
packed_bytes=75497472 where the plan is 1 and 37748736. After the fix the same run
reports 1 allocation / 36 MiB, and all four tiers plus an A->B->A interleave
through one shared workspace are bitwise identical to per-instance scratch.

CPU device is left untouched (no index to resolve).
